# Build context exclusions. Everything here either bloats the image, breaks
# the build, or leaks a secret.

# Reinstalled inside the image against the lockfile. Copying the host copy in
# would also ship Windows-built native binaries into a Linux container.
node_modules
.pnpm-store

# Built fresh in the builder stage. A stale host build would be copied over
# and then overwritten, costing upload time for nothing.
.next
out
build

# SECRETS. .env.local holds the real Google client id. If it reached the
# builder, Next would load it during `next build` and silently override the
# --build-arg values, so the image would be built against whatever this
# machine happens to have. The *.example files carry no values and are kept.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.docker.example

# History and tooling
.git
.gitignore
.vscode
.idea
.claude
*.log
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# Docs and container files: not read at build time
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
README.md
DOCKER.md
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
docs

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
